{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/index.html","title":"Overview and preface","text":"Rare BooksThe Padumāwati of Malik Muḥammad JāyasīEdited and translated by G. A. Grierson and Sudhakara Dvivedi (Bibliotheca Indica, 1911)Malik Muḥammad Jāyasī; edited by G. A. Grierson and Sudhakara Dvivedi <p>Rare Books</p> The Padumāwati of Malik Muḥammad Jāyasī <p>Edited and translated by G. A. Grierson and Sudhakara Dvivedi (Bibliotheca Indica, 1911)</p> <p>Malik Muḥammad Jāyasī; edited by G. A. Grierson and Sudhakara Dvivedi</p> <p>The Awadhī epic Padumāvata (1540) of the Sufi poet Jāyasī, on Padmāvatī and the siege of Chittor, edited with a translation and notes by Grierson and Dvivedi (Calcutta, 1896–1911).</p> Start reading <p>31 chapters</p>"},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/index.html#contents","title":"Contents","text":"<p>Chapters</p> <ul> <li>Pages 1–25</li> <li>Pages 26–50</li> <li>Pages 51–75</li> <li>Pages 76–100</li> <li>Pages 101–125</li> <li>Pages 126–150</li> <li>Pages 151–175</li> <li>Pages 176–200</li> <li>Pages 201–225</li> <li>Pages 226–250</li> <li>Pages 251–275</li> <li>Pages 276–300</li> <li>Pages 301–325</li> <li>Pages 326–350</li> <li>Pages 351–375</li> <li>Pages 376–400</li> <li>Pages 401–425</li> <li>Pages 426–450</li> <li>Pages 451–475</li> <li>Pages 476–500</li> <li>Pages 501–525</li> <li>Pages 526–550</li> <li>Pages 551–575</li> <li>Pages 576–600</li> <li>Pages 601–625</li> <li>Pages 626–650</li> <li>Pages 651–675</li> <li>Pages 676–700</li> <li>Pages 701–725</li> <li>Pages 726–750</li> <li>Pages 751–774</li> </ul>"},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/index.html#about-this-book","title":"About this book","text":"<p>The Awadhī epic Padumāvata (1540) of the Sufi poet Jāyasī, on Padmāvatī and the siege of Chittor, edited with a translation and notes by Grierson and Dvivedi (Calcutta, 1896–1911). Listed in the catalogue of the Rare Book Society of India.</p> <p>From Internet Archive · Public domain in India</p><p>Scanned from a copy in the Robarts Library, University of Toronto; hosted by the Internet Archive. Item: The Padumawati of Malik Muammad Jais · Malik Muhammad Jayasi, fl. 1540, Grierson, George Abraham, Sir, 1851-1941, Dvivedi, Sudhkara · 1911, 774 scanned pages. Published 1911; Malik Muḥammad Jāyasī lived in the sixteenth century, G. A. Grierson died 1941 and Sudhakara Dvivedi 1910; public domain in India.</p><p>This book is not stored in this library: its pages are shown from the Internet Archive when they are opened, in this library's own viewer, and each chapter ends with this credit. The pages are shown as scans in this library's viewer (zoom, pan, thumbnails); the text of this book is in a script the machine reading of the scans cannot yet give. The item on the Internet Archive (opened only if you click it).</p>"},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-1-25.html","title":"Pages 1–25","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-101-125.html","title":"Pages 101–125","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-126-150.html","title":"Pages 126–150","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-151-175.html","title":"Pages 151–175","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-176-200.html","title":"Pages 176–200","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-201-225.html","title":"Pages 201–225","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-226-250.html","title":"Pages 226–250","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-251-275.html","title":"Pages 251–275","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayasi-grierson/pages-26-50.html","title":"Pages 26–50","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/padumawati-jayas